<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37301" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏtĭn'</span></b> 
		is used, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> For
			potisne: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">potin' es? i. e. potes?</span>”
				
					<i>can you? are you able?</i>
				
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 2, 6, 6</span></i>
			; Plaut. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 7, 7,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			For potisne est? i. e. potest? potin' ut desinas? <i>can you leave off?</i> i. e. <i>pray leave
			off</i>, <i><span class="en">Ter. Ad. 4, 1, 23</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">potin' ut taceas?</span>”
				i. e. <i>be silent</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 4, 2, 94</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
